==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Eastwood''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Rodeo Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Cat Gunslinger can slow [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]] one at a time, while its targets are typically spawned in groups. He is thus only recommended for bosses like the [[Dark Cyclone]] and [[Razorback]]. It is best to try to form a stack before engaging enemies and work on keeping the frontline clear. Alternatively, he could be used alongside the more reliable [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] as an emergency second line of crowd-controllers. However, very few Dark enemies are Immune to Freeze, and those who aren't usually fall to [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], who can kill them outright, negating the purpose to use Cat Gunslinger in the first place.

==='''True Form'''===
Rodeo Cat gains higher stats and more notably, more range and longer Slow duration. However, he still lacks Area Attacks which hinders his performance against large swarms of Dark enemies. It's recommended to invest in this True Form if you wish to unlock Cat Gunslinger's [[Talents]].

==='''Talents'''===
Once he is given '''Target Relic''', his use is expanded to [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies in early [[Uncanny Legends]] stages and [[Charybdis' Mouth (Merciless)|Typhoon Nemo]]. His effectiveness remains limited due to Single Attacks, but he can at least do well at slowing [[Relic Bun-Bun]] and [[Primeval Cyclone]]. Later on, he is again outshined in this role by [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]], who has higher range and Area Attacks plus a ridiculously powerful True Form.

'''Attack Buff''' has little value, but '''HP Buff''', combined with '''Resist Curse''', can at least somewhat improve Rodeo Cat's usability against Relics. '''Recovery Speed Up''' is also important to facilitate stacking, since the slow chance is too low for his attack rate.

==='''Orb'''===
Its low health and damage, as well as a bad overall compatibility to Dark enemies make equipping any orb nigh pointless. In theory, a Relic defence orb might work, but due to Relic enemies' extreme damage output it is unlikely to make much of a difference.

A-grade curse resist orb with same talent unlocked for immunity.

